MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two fixes for #391 CI + review:

1. Green the release-readiness gate. Removing the implicit auto-migrate machinery
   lowered the D20 `bd` call-site counts (command 76→71; migrate.js 22→17), so the
   checked-in `bd-call-site-kill-list.md` audit artifact went stale and failed the
   `d20-audit-artifact-current` blocker cross-platform. Regenerated it from the
   canonical generator (renderBdCallSiteAuditMarkdown(auditBdCallSites(root))) so it
   matches the current tree.

2. CodeRabbit (beads-kernel-compat.js:123, Data Integrity, Major): the sidecar scan
   swallowed EVERY readdirSync failure as "no sidecars", so an EACCES/ENOTDIR scan
   error could hide sidecars silently — the exact data-loss class this migrator
   closes. detectUnmigratedSidecars now swallows only ENOENT (an absent candidate dir
   is normal) and returns real scan errors, which importBeadsSnapshot surfaces as a
   `sidecar-scan.<dir>` gap. TDD: a `.beads/backup` that is a FILE (ENOTDIR) now
   yields an honest gap instead of a silent skip.

Compat 28→ suite + release-readiness (64) green; eslint clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
